      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dinuclear Dy2 complex 2 is an SMM. The room-temperature χT product is 27.8 cm3 K mol−1 (per Dy2), decreasing to 13.7 cm3 K mol−1 at 1.8 K. In zero dc field the magnetization relaxes faster than 1.5×10−5 s at 1.85 K. Under an optimum 800 Oe dc field, thermally activated relaxation above 6 K follows an Arrhenius law with Δeff/kB = 27 K and τ0 = 5.6×10−7 s.",
