      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dinuclear Dy2 complex 3 is an SMM. Room-temperature χT is 28.0 cm3 K mol−1, falling to 17.6 cm3 K mol−1 at 1.8 K. A broad ac relaxation mode near 3 kHz at 1.85 K (zero dc field) appears to contain at least two contributions, attributed to the two independent DyIII sites. Below ~7–10 K quantum tunneling dominates (τ ≈ 4×10−4 s); above 11 K Arrhenius behavior gives a barrier of about 98 K with τ0 = 2.3×10−8 s. Applied dc fields accelerate the dynamics of 3.",
